{"id":"457b0a4b0a8d5081","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2024-12-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.7.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.7.0 introduced experimental `rockcraft remote-build`, which uses off-site compute and can build rocks for multiple architectures with one command.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-7/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:27.060073592Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"47ec3f6a14e20d82","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2024-12-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.7.0"},"statement":"To use `rockcraft remote-build` from a project containing a valid `rockcraft.yaml`, the project must be in a non-shallow Git repository and the user must have a Launchpad account; the prospective rock must also be open source and public.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-7/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:27.060073592Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"cfa1f93fe9c630be","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2024-12-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"24.04","version":"1.7.0"},"statement":"For projects targeting Ubuntu 24.04 and later, `rockcraft init` generates a project file with `base: ubuntu@24.04` by default, and the Django and Flask framework extensions support Gunicorn asynchronous workers.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-7/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:31.523290805Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"78e3bb6e7379e77a","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-01-31T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"24.04","version":"1.8.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.8 adds the `uv` Python-project plugin and the `jlink` Java-runtime plugin; for example, these parts select them with `plugin: uv` and `plugin: jlink` respectively.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-8/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:46.464317478Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"fccdcc2dfd8d4c88","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-02-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.9.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.9's `remote-build` command reports builds that are still pending and accepts `--project` to select a Launchpad project; for example, invoke `rockcraft remote-build --project my-launchpad-project`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-9/","added":"2026-10-25T21:55:55.966943306Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"748297a7edb6b6b3","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-04-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.10.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft-generated OCI rocks include the `org.opencontainers.image.description` annotation populated from the project summary and description.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-10/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:08.97354245Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"58c432f16276e581","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-05-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.11.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.11 adds the experimental `rockcraft test` command with a `test` init profile, and introduces `cargo-use` and `gradle` part plugins; for example, parts select the plugins using `plugin: cargo-use` and `plugin: gradle`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-11/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:18.939955784Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"df8a8bfd45bfb521","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-05-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.11.0"},"statement":"The Maven plugin accepts `maven-use-wrapper: true` to build using the Maven wrapper included in the source tree; for example, set `maven-use-wrapper: true` in a Maven part.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-11/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:23.101758647Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"2adfc57e0eff0764","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-06-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.12.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.12 sets the mediaType field in the image manifest of generated rocks.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-12/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:36.50367431Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e5f25edbbc105049","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-06-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.12.0"},"statement":"In Rockcraft 1.12, tests can use the CRAFT_ARTIFACT environment variable to obtain the full path to the rock file being tested.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-12/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:36.50367431Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"76969ae95a473381","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-07-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"25.10","version":"1.13.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.13 provides a second .NET plugin implementation for `ubuntu@25.10` projects and later; for example, a part on those bases selects the plugin with `plugin: dotnet`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-13/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:40.633618045Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"398fe748b584625a","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-08-29T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.14.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.14 adds the project-level `entrypoint-command` key; it replaces the rock’s default Pebble OCI entrypoint and OCI CMD.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-14/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:52.133157861Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3d9fc06d271879d6","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-08-29T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.14.0"},"statement":"`entrypoint-command` is a string-valued project key; for example, `entrypoint-command: /usr/bin/my-app`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-14/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:52.133157861Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c683fdbbf18777e5","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-08-29T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.14.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.14 adds the JLink plugin key `jlink-extra-modules` for adding Java modules to its generated OpenJDK runtime; for example, a JLink part can set `jlink-extra-modules: [jdk.crypto.ec]`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-14/","added":"2026-10-25T21:56:56.581041942Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d46ca30bfb7e6c58","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"25.10","version":"1.15.0"},"statement":"For `ubuntu@25.10` and later projects, the Python plugin has a new implementation with improved usrmerge compatibility, selectable as the base-specific Python plugin; for example, use `plugin: python` in a Python part with `base: ubuntu@25.10`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-15/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:03.915184156Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7f1b327061c25606","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"20.04","version":"1.15.0"},"statement":"In Rockcraft 1.15.0, packing a rock on an unmaintained base halts by default; to proceed, run `rockcraft pack --ignore=unmaintained`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-15/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:14.0560508Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"32b6c0e6fddf5d95","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"20.04","version":"1.15.0"},"statement":"At Rockcraft 1.15.0’s release, Ubuntu 20.04 was an affected unmaintained base, whose standard support ended on 2025-05-31; the documented way to proceed is the `--ignore=unmaintained` option, not setting `build-base: ubuntu@24.04`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-15/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:14.0560508Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d40287b146ace26b","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.15.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft project names may be a single character from release 1.15 onward; for example, `name: x` meets the minimum name length.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-15/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:20.972826317Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4c2ddc0dc3c2ea72","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-12-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.16.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.16 supports `ubuntu@26.04` as a development base only when the project sets `build-base: devel`, while `ubuntu@25.10` becomes fully supported and no longer requires that setting; for example, `base: ubuntu@26.04` with `build-base: devel`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-16/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:33.433157054Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"848a424bf3465da5","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2025-12-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.16.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft platform names no longer permit the forward-slash character; for example, use `platforms: {amd64: {build-on: [amd64]}}` rather than a slash-containing platform key.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-16/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:38.158368514Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3a01d867dc7c3e1c","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-02-09T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.17.0"},"statement":"The `uv` part plugin compiles Python bytecode by default; a part can disable that behavior by setting `build-environment: [{UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE: \"0\"}]`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-17/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:46.755142415Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a511678a34f67abd","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-02-09T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.17.0"},"statement":"The 12-factor app extension init profiles use `base: bare` to create leaner rocks, and extension-generated rocks include a command interpreter at `/bin/sh`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-17/","added":"2026-10-25T21:57:55.05303919Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"cbaf48c5f37854b6","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.18.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.18 adds `override-overlay` to part configuration, which runs a Bash script directly on the overlay system; for example, add `override-overlay: |\\n  apt-get update` to a part.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-18/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:10.888425487Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ffc9a759104f51f3","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"25.10","version":"1.18.0"},"statement":"Projects targeting `ubuntu@25.10` and later can use the new .NET plugin implementation, which exposes more control over distinct .NET build steps; select it in a part with `plugin: dotnet`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-18/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:16.064468558Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ce2189b2964277bc","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-05-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.19.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.19 supports `ubuntu@26.04` as a stable base without requiring `build-base: devel`; for example, a project can set `base: ubuntu@26.04`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-19/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:23.023005962Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"75cba1eb0e6867ed","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-05-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"24.04","version":"1.19.0"},"statement":"The Express, FastAPI and Go 12-factor extensions are stable and no longer require `ROCKCRAFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_EXTENSIONS`; for example, enable the Go extension with `extensions: [go-framework]`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-19/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:29.25641805Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"978c5b90194a46f3","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-05-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"25.10","version":"1.19.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.19 adds the Bazel part plugin for rocks targeting `ubuntu@25.10` and later; for example, a Bazel-based part declares `plugin: bazel`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-19/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:34.908488746Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6960ddb063dc5deb","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-07-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.10","version":"1.20.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.20 supports the `ubuntu@26.10` base as a development base when the project sets `build-base: devel`; for example, `base: ubuntu@26.10` with `build-base: devel`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-20/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:40.813598984Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"98841652b9afde73","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-07-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.20.0"},"statement":"On `ubuntu@26.04`, the Flask, Django, FastAPI, Go, Express and Spring Boot framework extensions are experimental, require `ROCKCRAFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_EXTENSIONS=1`, put application content in `/app`, and provide writable `/app-data`; extension implementation selection uses `build-base` when set and otherwise `base`, and `base: bare` requires `build-base`. For example, `base: ubuntu@26.04` and `extensions: [flask-framework]` use that implementation.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-20/","added":"2026-10-25T21:58:46.873214091Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"f5a11b8648492891","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21 adds the `stage-slices` part key for declaring Chisel slices to install into a part's install directory; for example, `stage-slices: [libc6_libs, base-files_bin]`. Slices may still be declared through `stage-packages` for bases through `ubuntu@26.10`, but that compatibility is dropped starting with `ubuntu@27.04`.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:39.163923196Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1e3ec2bf2536fe9c","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"24.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21's Flask, Django, and FastAPI 12-factor extensions support Python projects that use uv; for example, select `extensions: [fastapi-framework]` for a FastAPI project whose Python dependencies are managed with uv.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:43.926323226Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3cabb980c5975fc9","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21 adds `rockcraft init --vcs` to initialize a Git repository when creating a project.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:58.245921921Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c25053d6dcd51fdc","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"For an example on ubuntu@22.04, run `rockcraft init --profile simple --vcs`; `bare` is not an init profile.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:58.245921921Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bfd41dfb5707f67f","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21 supports experimental packing of a project whose `rockcraft.yaml` is below the Git repository root when `ROCKCRAFT_EXPERIMENTAL_MONOREPO` is set; for example, run `ROCKCRAFT_EXPERIMENTAL_MONOREPO=1 rockcraft pack` from the nested project directory.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:46:04.459243908Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"2504a48a7b5a748d","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21 skips re-packing a rock when the project has not changed since the previous pack.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:46:20.879152633Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a42bc3d974f060d4","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"In rocks built by Rockcraft 1.21, `/var/lib/pebble/default/` has the sticky bit set so that users cannot remove or rename entries created by other users.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:46:33.230181959Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7b25e8aa17718b58","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"For 12-factor framework extensions on `ubuntu@26.04`, Rockcraft selects the extension implementation according to `build-base` when set, and otherwise according to `base`; for example, a project with `base: ubuntu@26.04` and `build-base: ubuntu@24.04` selects the Ubuntu 24.04 extension implementation.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:46:58.318499864Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"89e8dc498f2c5709","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"On Ubuntu 26.04, the Flask, Django, FastAPI, Go, Express, and Spring Boot extensions are experimental and require `ROCKCRAFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_EXTENSIONS=1`; they place application content under `/app` and create `/app-data`, owned by `_daemon_` and writable by the application service, for application-generated data. `/app-data` is in the container filesystem, so its contents do not persist across container replacement unless a volume is mounted there.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/reference/extensions/","added":"2026-10-25T23:47:23.817432383Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"79d191dfc00d78d8","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"For a Rockcraft 1.21 project with `base: bare`, `build-base` is mandatory for framework extension dispatch; for example, `base: bare` with `build-base: ubuntu@24.04` selects the stable Ubuntu 24.04 extension implementation without requiring the experimental extensions environment variable.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/reference/extensions/","added":"2026-10-25T23:47:33.241492514Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ce0f92c51562a7a0","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.21.2"},"statement":"For bare-based rocks using the Go or Express.js 12-factor extension, Rockcraft 1.21.2 stages the `base-files_tmp` Chisel slice, which provides `/tmp`.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/rockcraft/releases/tag/1.21.2","added":"2026-10-25T23:47:50.482324493Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"91f1e238d8fb1c62","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26.04","version":"1.21.2"},"statement":"For a bare-based Express.js rock, configure `extensions: [expressjs-framework]` (not `extensions: [express-framework]`).","source":"https://github.com/canonical/rockcraft/releases/tag/1.21.2","added":"2026-10-25T23:47:50.482324493Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"226d3b9dc0b813a8","subject":"rockcraft","time":"2026-10-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22.04","version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"Rockcraft 1.21 accepts `@` to specify versions for Debian packages and snaps in `build-packages`, `stage-packages`, `build-snaps`, and `stage-snaps`; for example, a part can use `stage-packages: [libfoo@1.2]` and `build-snaps: [tool@2.0]`. The previous version notation remains supported through `ubuntu@26.10`, but future bases require the `@` notation.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/rockcraft/stable/release-notes/rockcraft-1-21/","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:30.313602402Z","by":"user"}
